.\" Manual page for the optional DistroForge Typer facade.
.\" The command list, the argument names, the defaults and the exit statuses
.\" documented here are derived from distroforge/typer_cli.py and confirmed
.\" against the generated `--help` output, not written from memory.
.TH distroforge\-typer 1 2026-07-26 "DistroForge 0.3.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
distroforge-typer \- launch the DistroForge Typer entry point
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B distroforge\-typer
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.PP
.B distroforge\-typer legacy
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B distroforge\-typer
is an optional, deliberately narrow facade over
.BR distroforge (1).
It exposes 29 commands \(em the ones used most often \(em with Typer's
completion, coloured help and strict argument parsing, and forwards everything
else to the classic parser.
.PP
It adds no capability of its own: every command below builds an argument list
and hands it to the same code path
.B distroforge
uses, so behaviour, safety model and reports are identical. The advanced surface
is intentionally
.I not
mirrored here; use
.B distroforge\-typer legacy
or
.BR distroforge (1)
for it.
.PP
Typer is an optional dependency. When it is not installed this program prints
how to obtain it and exits without doing anything.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Project and catalogs
.TP
.BR releases ", " source\-starters
List the bundled release catalog and the project source starters.
.B source\-starters
accepts
.B \-\-release
and
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.BR new " \fINAME ROOT\fR"
Create a project.
.B \-\-release
defaults to
.BR 26.04 ;
.BR \-\-starter ,
.B \-\-source\-iso
and
.B \-\-previous\-project
select the source.
.TP
.BR profile\-diff " \fIROOT PROFILE\fR"
Diff a project against a package profile.
.B \-\-json
emits the machine\-readable form.
.TP
.BR plugins " \fIROOT\fR"
List the local plugins of a project.
.SS Host readiness
.TP
.B doctor
Check host tooling.
.BR \-\-python ,
.BR \-\-debian\-dev ,
.BR \-\-fix\-python ,
.BR \-\-install ,
.B \-\-include\-optional
and
.B \-\-no\-sudo
map one\-to\-one onto the
.B distroforge doctor
flags.
.TP
.BR mirrors\-doctor " \fIROOT\fR"
Diagnose the APT mirror layer.
.B \-\-definition
and
.B \-\-json
are accepted.
.SS Reviewing and building
.TP
.BR readiness " \fIROOT\fR, " dry\-run\-report " \fIROOT\fR, " explain\-risk " \fIROOT\fR, " ux\-audit " \fIROOT\fR, " ai\-review " \fIROOT\fR"
The review surfaces. All accept
.BR \-\-definition ;
all but
.B explain\-risk
also accept
.BR \-\-json ,
and
.B dry\-run\-report
accepts
.BR \-\-no\-command\-simulation .
.TP
.BR explain " \fIROOT\fR"
Explain in plain language what a build of that project would do.
.B \-\-json
emits the machine\-readable form and
.B \-\-strict
promotes advisory findings to blocking ones.
.TP
.BR build\-phases
Print the build phase contracts.
.B \-\-stage
scopes the catalog to one pipeline stage.
.TP
.BR build " \fIROOT\fR"
Run or dry\-run a build with the small common option set:
.BR \-\-source\-iso ,
.BR \-\-desktop ,
.BR \-\-execute ,
.B \-\-no\-sudo
and
.BR \-\-ci .
It stays a dry\-run without
.BR \-\-execute .
The other 186 build options are not mirrored here; reach them through
.B distroforge\-typer legacy
or
.BR distroforge (1).
.SS Branding and debranding
.TP
.BR branding\-audit " \fIROOT\fR"
Audit branding compliance.
.B \-\-mode
defaults to
.BR internal ;
.B \-\-definition
and
.B \-\-json
are accepted.
.TP
.BR branding\-validate " \fIROOT\fR, " branding\-clearance " \fIROOT\fR"
Validate branding or write a clearance report.
.B \-\-mode
defaults to
.B redistributable
for both;
.B branding\-clearance
also accepts
.BR \-\-output .
.TP
.BR branding\-preview " \fIROOT\fR"
Render branding previews.
.B \-\-target
defaults to
.BR all ;
.B \-\-output\-dir
selects the destination.
.TP
.BR debrand\-scan " \fIROOT\fR"
Scan a source ISO for upstream identity text.
.SS Recipes and presets
.TP
.BR guided\-recipe " [\fINAME\fR], " glossary " [\fITERM\fR]"
List or render the guided recipe prompts, and explain the domain vocabulary.
.TP
.BR export\-recipe " \fIROOT TARGET\fR, " export\-build\-preset " \fIROOT TARGET\fR"
Export the project as a reusable recipe or a maintainer build preset.
.B export\-build\-preset
accepts
.BR \-\-channel ,
.B \-\-revision
and
.BR \-\-notes .
.SS Advisory
.TP
.BR forgeadvisor\-review\-build " \fIROOT\fR, " forgeadvisor\-explain\-log " \fILOG\fR, " forgeadvisor\-doctor\-ai
The three most used advisory verbs. They explain and cite; they never build,
sign or apply anything. The remaining advisory subcommands are reached through
.B distroforge\-typer legacy
or
.BR distroforge (1).
.SS Escape hatch and desktop
.TP
.BR legacy " [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]"
Forward every remaining argument verbatim to
.BR distroforge (1),
unparsed. This is how the full 84\-command, 292\-option surface stays reachable
from this entry point.
.TP
.B gui
Launch the Qt desktop interface; equivalent to
.BR distroforge\-gui (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the command list, or the options of one command, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-completion
Install shell completion for the current shell.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-completion
Print the completion script for the current shell instead of installing it.
.SS Option conventions
Typer derives the option names from the Python parameter names, so an option is
always the parameter name with underscores replaced by dashes, and it pairs
every boolean option with a generated negative form
.RB ( \-\-execute
implies
.BR \-\-no\-execute ).
The positive form is what the underlying
.BR distroforge (1)
verb receives; the negative form only restores the default.
.PP
.B \-\-json
is the machine\-readable output switch, exactly as in
.BR distroforge (1).
.B \-\-definition
loads an image definition before the command\-line values.
.B \-\-execute
is the only way to leave dry\-run mode.
.PP
This facade rejects options it does not declare. An unknown flag is an error
here, not a pass\-through; use
.B distroforge\-typer legacy
when the option you need lives only on the classic parser.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed.
.TP
.B 1
Typer is not installed. The message names the optional extra to install and the
.B "python3 \-m distroforge"
fallback.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, or a handled runtime failure forwarded from
.BR distroforge (1):
an unknown or misused option, a missing file or directory, malformed JSON or
YAML, or a project that does not exist.
.PP
.B gui
propagates the exit status of the Qt application.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B distroforge\-typer
introduces no variable of its own. It honours the whole environment of
.BR distroforge (1),
in particular
.BR DISTROFORGE_PRIVILEGE ,
.BR SUDO_ASKPASS ,
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
and
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME .
Typer additionally honours the standard
.B NO_COLOR
and
.B TERM
conventions when rendering its help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I PROJECT/project.json
The project description read and written by every command that takes a
.I ROOT
argument.
.TP
.I PROJECT/dist/
Host output directory for the reports these commands produce.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/distroforge/
Installed documentation.
.PP
The files of
.BR distroforge (1)
apply unchanged; this entry point owns no state of its own.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a project and review it:
.PP
.EX
distroforge\-typer new MyDistro ~/DistroForge/MyDistro \-\-release 26.04
distroforge\-typer readiness ~/DistroForge/MyDistro \-\-json
distroforge\-typer explain ~/DistroForge/MyDistro
.EE
.PP
Dry\-run then execute a small build:
.PP
.EX
distroforge\-typer build ~/DistroForge/MyDistro \-\-desktop ubuntu_minimal
distroforge\-typer build ~/DistroForge/MyDistro \-\-desktop ubuntu_minimal \-\-execute
.EE
.PP
Reach an option this facade does not declare:
.PP
.EX
distroforge\-typer legacy build ~/DistroForge/MyDistro \\
    \-\-vuln\-scan \-\-vuln\-policy block\-critical \-\-sbom\-format spdx
.EE
.PP
Install shell completion:
.PP
.EX
distroforge\-typer \-\-install\-completion
.EE
.PP
Install the optional dependency when the launcher reports it is missing:
.PP
.EX
sudo apt install python3\-typer
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR distroforge (1),
.BR distroforge\-gui (1)
.PP
See
.I /usr/share/doc/distroforge/docs/gui\-parity.md
for the full command surface and
.I docs/debian\-ubuntu\-python\-policy.md
for how the optional Python dependencies are expressed.
.SH BUGS
DistroForge 0.3.5 is alpha software. This facade covers 29 of the 84 commands on
purpose; treat
.BR distroforge (1)
as the reference surface.
.PP
DistroForge is an independent project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by
Canonical. Ubuntu is mentioned solely as a compatible target distribution.
